### Description

Spigot/Bukkit/CraftBukkit no longer contains the strange version 'classifier' (i.e. v1_21_R1) in the packages.

Because of this the below method now fails to resolve a Minecraft version on versions 26.1.x.

https://github.com/lucko/spark/blob/1b42ef3390a3faf4f121bb0629df51d041af15ea/spark-bukkit/src/main/java/me/lucko/spark/bukkit/BukkitPlatformInfo.java#L57

A possible solution to this may be simply use the SharedConstants class found under the `net.minecraft` package, though there may be a better solution to this and this recommendation may not return the correct information required.
```java
try {
    final Class<?> clazz = Class.forName("net.minecraft.SharedConstants");
    final Field currentVersion = clazz.getDeclaredField("CURRENT_VERSION");
    currentVersion.setAccessible(true);
    Class<?> ver = currentVersion.getType();
    System.out.println(ver.getDeclaredMethod("name").invoke(currentVersion.get(this)));
} catch (Exception e) {
    // ignore
}
```

### Reproduction Steps

Launch a Spigot server with Spark placed in the plugins folder.
Execute `/spark profiler open`.
The error occurs. 


### Expected Behaviour

Running `/spark profiler open` or `/spark profiler stop` would complete successfully, sending the profiler link.

### Platform Information

* Minecraft Version: 26.1.2
* Platform Type: Server
* Platform Brand: Spigot
* Platform Version: 4626-Spigot-566f972-b5ccd9c


### Spark Version

1.10.172

### Logs and Configs

https://gist.github.com/ItsSchatten/3edb540b1c4f43d1d75930abfb527856

### Extra Details

_No response_

Server software: Forge-1.19.2-43.2.1 ; Java 17

